-- title:
--   Extending κ-automorphisms to a separable constant-field extension
-- statement:
--   Let $\kappa$ be a field and $F$ a field that is a $\kappa$-algebra. Let $\kappa'$ be a field extension of $\kappa$ that is algebraic and separable over $\kappa$, and let $F'$ be a field carrying algebra structures over $\kappa'$, over $F$ and over $\kappa$, the latter compatible with the other two in the sense that $\kappa \to F \to F'$ and $\kappa \to \kappa' \to F'$ both compose to the structure map $\kappa \to F'$. Assume two hypotheses: first, every element of $F$ that is algebraic over $\kappa$ lies in the image of the structure map $\kappa \to F$ (so that $\kappa$ is, up to this identification, algebraically closed in $F$); second, the $F$-subalgebra of $F'$ generated by the image of $\kappa' \to F'$ is all of $F'$, i.e. $F'$ is generated over $F$ by the image of $\kappa'$. Then for every $\kappa$-algebra automorphism $\sigma$ of $F$ there exists a $\kappa'$-algebra automorphism $\sigma'$ of $F'$ — in particular one fixing the image of $\kappa'$ pointwise — such that $\sigma'(\iota(f)) = \iota(\sigma f)$ for all $f \in F$, where $\iota \colon F \to F'$ is the structure map.
--
--   This is the standard statement that automorphisms of a regular extension (here: one in which the base field is algebraically closed) extend to a separable algebraic constant-field extension, the extension being trivial on the new constants. It is used in the analysis of inertia at $p$ for the modular curves $X_0(p)$, $X_1(p)$, where automorphisms of a function field over $\mathbb{F}_p$ must be transported to the corresponding field over an algebraic extension of constants.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgEquiv_exists_extend_of_forall_isAlgebraic_mem_range_of_adjoin_range_eq_top.lean

